 * `script`: Use a bootstrap that uses an arbitrary executable script (usually a
   shell script) instead of requiring it be a Python program.
 
+* `native`: With Bzlmod, start the standard Python bootstrap with a native
+  executable and the declared interpreter. Windows, custom shebangs and
+  custom bootstrap templates retain the existing bootstrap. The worker
+  must be able to run the interpreter and supply a physical runfiles tree.
+
+:::{versionadded} VERSION_NEXT_FEATURE
+Added the opt-in native bootstrap.
+:::
+
